Here's an idea that will effectively shut down the _misuse_
of wands of polymorph: replace wands of polymorph with
the something like the "wand of wonder" of moria! For 
non-Moria players, a wand of wonder, when zapped, picks
some wand effect at random. For the purposes of NetHack,
let us say that  a wand of "metamorph" sometimes has
a temporary effect on itself. So the implications:

o you could cancel the wands you're metamorphing 
o you could burn up all the scrolls/spellbooks and 
  boil away/freeze potions you're metamorphing
o you could kill yourself with bouncing death rays
o you could teleport all your neat piles to various parts
  of your level (I really like this!).

Add to this the possibility of lightning and fire destroying
armor as well, and you could make metamorphing objects an
act of desperation, rather than any kind of sure-fire way
to win. My problem with the other proposals is:

o they involve changing code at different places - this
would involve only the spell-zapping code,
o they (the polymorphing randomly destroys objects proposal)
can be beaten by sheer volume.

